# Fixture and certificate bytes are normative.
#
# Every port hashes these files and compares the digest against the one
# fixtures/cases.json records, so the bytes have to be identical on every
# checkout. Git's default line-ending translation rewrites a text file on a
# Windows working copy, which changes those bytes and fails the registry
# check for anything it touches. It already did: the Go and .NET suites both
# failed on windows-latest over fixtures/public-receipts/LICENSE-upstream,
# and nowhere else.
#
# -text disables that translation. It is not about whether a file looks like
# text; it is about whether its bytes are load-bearing. These are.
fixtures/** -text
certs/** -text
*.der -text
*.cer -text
*.b64 -text
*.jws -text
*.hex -text
